  "assertion_assessments": [
    {
      "id": "HW01",
      "anchors_inspected": 2,
      "assessment": "The Howell sentence matches both retained p.68 images, including its Friday/Saturday/Sunday progression. Neither inspected paragraph attaches a footnote marker to the Howell clause. The 1903 title image distinguishes the 1902 title date from the 1903 GPO imprint. Edition agreement does not identify the underlying account or add an independent witness.",
      "status": "accepted_as_bounded_source_attribution",
      "required_finding_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "HW02",
      "anchors_inspected": 1,
      "assessment": "The selected p.5 passage matches the retained image and the Cornelius Cadle signature. Its report comparison, Washington searches, interviews and missing/meager reports are the commission's methodological account, not an incident-specific source attribution.",
      "status": "accepted_as_bounded_source_attribution",
      "required_finding_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "HW03",
      "anchors_inspected": 2,
      "assessment": "All three Medkirk sections match p.537. Editorial attribution names Co. E, 72d Ohio and March 22d, 1886. The selected letter distinguishes frequent fire, enemy return fire toward evening, a cavalry brush and an officer party riding away. The record does not infer continuous combat, general termination, exact enemy formation, Reed dependence or a Sunday connection.",
      "status": "accepted_as_bounded_source_attribution",
      "required_finding_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "HW04",
      "anchors_inspected": 4,
      "assessment": "All five Worthington sections match pp.137 and 140. Sharpe's heading, about-7-a.m. expulsion and all-day house occupation are correctly separated; the Crary selection and its parenthetical September date are retained. Sherman's denial is also preserved. These remain disputed selections in one adversarial publication, not authenticated original transcripts or reconciled positions.",
      "status": "accepted_as_bounded_source_attribution",
      "required_finding_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "HW05",
      "anchors_inspected": 2,
      "assessment": "Both Abstract sections match p.4: item 20 cites pp.44 and 47, and another passage describes a copy of proceedings sent from Washington. The item is treated as disputed testimony within the author's adversarial presentation, not as an adopted denial. The title's August 14, 1862 trial date is not adopted as a printing date. The inspected p.4 reference to fighting at Fredericksburgh and Vicksburgh supports retaining publication chronology as unknown.",
      "status": "accepted_as_bounded_source_attribution",
      "required_finding_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "HW06",
      "anchors_inspected": 1,
      "assessment": "The selected text matches the retained NPS HTML under Historic Plaque #O and Inscription Reads. I read the entire displayed inscription, which does not name Howell. This supports the narrow negative claim about one modern transcription, not a conclusion about all tablets, the original plaque, first shots or whether Saturday contact happened.",
      "status": "accepted_as_bounded_source_attribution",
      "required_finding_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "HW07",
      "anchors_inspected": 2,
      "assessment": "The selected NARA passages match retained HTML under the Shiloh headings in sections 92.10.5 and 79.10.2. The correspondence date ranges are accurately preserved. These are record-series leads, with no demonstrated Howell-specific contents, item locator, digitization status or access exhaustion.",
      "status": "accepted_as_bounded_source_attribution",
      "required_finding_ids": []
    }
  ],
